===Etymology===
From {{der|se|urj-pro|-}} negative verb stem {{m|urj-pro|*e-}} ~ {{m|urj-pro|*ä-}} ~ {{m|urj-pro|*a-}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|ei}}, {{cog|fi|ei}}, and {{cog|sms|ij}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{se-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{head|se|verb}}

# [[not]]

====Usage notes====
''ii'' is a [[defective verb]] and is only inflected for person and the indicative and imperative moods. The main verb is inflected in the [[connegative]] form and contains information about tense and mood:
: {{ux|se|Son '''ii''' dieđe.|She '''does not''' know.}}
: {{ux|se|Son '''ii''' diehtán.|She '''did not''' know.}}
: {{ux|se|Son '''ii''' dieđáše.|She '''would not''' know.}}

When a sentence structure requires the verb to be in a different form (e.g. in the infinitive), the negator will be moved elsewhere:
: {{ux|se|Son lohká ahte son '''ii''' dieđe.|She says that she '''does not''' know.}}
: {{ux|se|Son '''ii''' loga iežas diehtit.|She says she '''does not''' know.|lit=She '''does not''' say herself to know.}}

